---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import FeatureCard from '@components/ui/FeatureCard.astro'
import CareersForm from '@components/forms/CareersForm.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Careers at Voxivium — Roles we're starting to fill"
  description="Voxivium is pre-launch and meeting candidates now so we know who to call when funding allows the next hire. Three roles, equity-only compensation, and a PBC structure that codifies internal commitments."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Careers</p>
      <h1>Help us build political accountability.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Voxivium is a pre-launch Public Benefit Corporation. We're meeting candidates now so that
        when funding allows the next hire, we already know who to call.
      </p>

      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <span class="toc-label">On this page</span>
        <a href="#timing">A note on timing</a>
        <a href="#culture">What we look for</a>
        <a href="#compensation">Compensation</a>
        <a href="#roles">Open roles</a>
        <a href="#apply">Apply</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="timing" id="timing">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>A note on timing</h2>
      <p>
        We're not actively filling any of the roles below today. Voxivium is pre-revenue and
        pre-launch. We're collecting applications now because the platform is close to launch and
        when funding allows the next hire, we'd rather already know who you are than start a search
        from scratch.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you submit, we'll reply when there's something concrete to discuss. That may be soon. It
        may not be.  We'd rather not pretend otherwise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="culture" id="culture">
    <div class="container">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">What we look for</p>
        <h2>Versatile, mission-aligned, comfortable building.</h2>
      </header>

      <div class="grid">
        <FeatureCard title="Versatility over specialization">
          <p>
            The team is small. Every hire spans more than one discipline. The right candidate
            shows up with one core strength and adjacent abilities they'll use weekly, not
            quarterly.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>
        <FeatureCard title="Mission alignment">
          <p>
            The work is civic infrastructure. You'll be making decisions about methodology,
            partisan balance, privacy, and trust where the right answer rarely shows up in a
            startup playbook. Caring about the mission is not a tiebreaker — it's the job.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>
        <FeatureCard title="Comfort with ambiguity">
          <p>
            Pre-launch means decisions get made with incomplete information, often by the person
            doing the work. We need people who can make a call, document it, and revisit it
            without ego.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>
        <FeatureCard title="Non-partisan rigor">
          <p>
            Voxivium's value depends on being trusted across the spectrum. Candidates who can hold
            that line in their public footprint and their day-to-day reasoning have a meaningful
            edge.
          </p>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="compensation" id="compensation">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Compensation</h2>
      <p>
        Voxivium is pre-revenue. Compensation is currently equity-only, with cash compensation to
        follow funding. We won't pretend that's not a real ask. It is.
      </p>
      <p>
        The equity comes with PBC governance you won't find at most startups, codified in our
        corporate bylaws:
      </p>
      <ul class="commitments">
        <li>
          <strong>5:1 executive-to-employee pay ratio cap.</strong> Total compensation between the
          highest-paid executive and the lowest-paid employee is capped at 5:1.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Locality-adjusted living wage for all staff.</strong> No exceptions, no roles
          excluded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Employee profit sharing.</strong> After necessary operational reserves, profits
          are shared with the people who built the platform.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="roles" id="roles">
    <div class="container">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Open roles</p>
        <h2>Three positions we're hiring next.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Each of these covers more ground than a typical job title implies. That's deliberate.
        </p>
      </header>

      <article class="role">
        <h3>Support, QA, and Deployment Engineer</h3>
        <p class="role-summary">
          The platform engineer who keeps users unblocked and the system shipping. You'll own the
          loop from "user reports a problem" to "fix is live in production."
        </p>
        <h4>What you'd do</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Handle user-reported issues end-to-end: reproduce, diagnose, fix or hand off, communicate back.</li>
          <li>Own quality assurance: write and run the regression tests, build the smoke tests, catch what slips past automated checks.</li>
          <li>Run deployments: ship code to production safely, roll back when needed, keep release notes honest.</li>
          <li>Improve the engineering toolchain over time — CI, monitoring, alerting — when the gap is felt.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>What we look for</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Comfort across web stack, cloud infrastructure (AWS preferred), and shell.</li>
          <li>Real experience handling production incidents and the patience to write good post-mortems.</li>
          <li>QA instinct: the urge to break your own work before it ships.</li>
          <li>Strong written communication.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="role-note">Currently equity-only. Full-time, remote-first.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="role">
        <h3>Marketing, Pricing, and Sales</h3>
        <p class="role-summary">
          The commercial lead who turns interest into revenue. You'll own pricing decisions, public
          positioning, and the B2B sales motion for media, research, and AI partners.
        </p>
        <h4>What you'd do</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Develop the pricing strategy across politician, media/research, and AI lab tiers. Test, adjust, document the why.</li>
          <li>Represent the public face of Voxivium: press relationships, partner conversations, conference presence.</li>
          <li>Run the sales pipeline for media organizations, academic researchers, and AI alignment teams.</li>
          <li>Maintain the non-partisan brand integrity that makes the platform valuable. Every word ships through this filter.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>What we look for</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Track record selling complex B2B products — ideally data, API, or platform sales.</li>
          <li>Strong instinct for pricing data businesses; comfortable with both subscription and tiered-access models.</li>
          <li>Ability to write the way smart customers want to read. No jargon, no hype, no partisan tells.</li>
          <li>Bonus: existing relationships in journalism, academia, civic tech, or AI safety.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="role-note">Currently equity-only. Full-time, remote-first.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="role">
        <h3>Policy &amp; Content Specialist</h3>
        <p class="role-summary">
          The editorial conscience of the platform. You'll review the plain-English summaries of
          legislation, court rulings, and executive actions that voters read and that determine
          whether they trust us.
        </p>
        <h4>What you'd do</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Review neutral, accurate, plain-English summaries of bills, votes, court rulings, and executive orders at the federal level — and over time, state and local.</li>
          <li>Define and refine the methodology for issue categorization, including how partisan framing is filtered out before it reaches users.</li>
          <li>Review algorithmic position recommendations for bias and surface any drift to the team.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>What we look for</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Background in legislative journalism, policy research, legislative-aide work, or political science — anyone whose job has been reading bills and explaining them clearly.</li>
          <li>Demonstrably non-partisan writing record. We'll read your work.</li>
          <li>Fast, precise editing under tight deadlines.</li>
          <li>Engineering literacy is a plus, not a requirement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="role-note">Currently equity-only. Full-time, remote-first.</p>
      </article>

      <p class="other-note">
        Don't see a role that fits but think you'd add something? Select <em>Other</em> in the
        application form below and tell us where you'd fit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="apply" id="apply">
    <div class="container">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Apply</p>
        <h2>Send us your resume.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          We extract a plain-text version of your PDF for review. The original file is not stored.
          You'll receive a confirmation that we've received your application; we'll follow up when
          there's something to discuss.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="form-card">
        <CareersForm />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script
    is:inline
    src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js"
    async
    defer></script>

  <script>
    import '@lib/forms/client'
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 10vh, 6rem) 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 1.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  h4 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .page-hero .lead {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .toc {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .toc-label {
    color: var(--color-brand-text3);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }

  .toc a {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.625rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-brand-el1);
    background: var(--color-brand-bg);
    transition:
      background-color 150ms ease,
      border-color 150ms ease;
  }

  .toc a:hover {
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border-color: var(--color-brand-el2);
  }

  .toc a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-brand-primary);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .timing,
  .compensation,
  .roles,
  .apply {
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vh, 4rem) 1.5rem;
  }

  .culture {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem) 1.5rem;
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-brand-el1);
  }

  .timing p,
  .compensation p,
  .compensation ul {
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .compensation ul.commitments {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.875rem;
  }

  .compensation ul.commitments li {
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .compensation ul.commitments li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.7em;
    width: 0.5rem;
    height: 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-brand-primary);
  }

  .compensation strong {
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
  }

  .timing .container,
  .culture .container,
  .compensation .container,
  .roles .container,
  .apply .container {
    max-width: 64rem;
  }

  header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .lead {
    margin: 1rem auto 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-text3);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .role {
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-brand-el1);
    border-radius: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .role:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .role-summary {
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .role ul {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .role ul li {
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
  }

  .role-note {
    color: var(--color-brand-text3);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
  }

  .other-note {
    margin: 2rem auto 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-text3);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .form-card {
    background: var(--color-brand-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-brand-el1);
    border-radius: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
</style>
